# Environment boundary

- Default local instructions to Windows PowerShell 7 and label them clearly.
- Use Git Bash only when a command is explicitly intended as Bash/POSIX syntax.
- Treat Git Bash as compatibility, not proof of a Linux or Vercel build.
- Keep source portable: no hard-coded drive paths, `.cmd` assumptions, or
  case-insensitive imports in application/runtime code.
- Use UTF-8 without BOM and LF for shared source and Linux/runtime files.
- Use CRLF only for Windows-only `.ps1`, `.cmd`, and `.bat` entrypoints.
- Verify relevant changes locally on Windows and in Linux CI.
